{
  "requirement": "When a model tool explicitly reads an excluded file, the harness MUST return a tool error naming the path and the reason\nit cannot be read, add no evidence input, and continue the assessment.\nDiscovery and search MUST omit excluded files. Malformed tool\narguments and ordinary read failures MUST also return explanatory tool errors.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap in `requirements.authoring.read_denial`. I judged this from the supplied test sources and did not request any implementation source.\n\n**1. An explicit read of an excluded file returns a tool error naming the path and reason, adds no evidence input, and the assessment continues.**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[explicit_ignored_reads_return_an_error_and_the_assessment_continues]` is an end-to-end test. A model `habeas` call reads a gitignored `untracked.txt`.\n  - The second request to the model contains `untracked.txt` and \"excluded\", but not the file's content.\n  - Two requests are made, so the assessment continued, and the run completes.\n  - `tool_failures` records one `habeas` failure.\n  - The evidence output does not mention the file.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[a_denied_read_returns_an_error_and_its_assessment_continues]` runs a batch with a denied read. The denied subject makes a second request, every subject completes with a true determination, and the denied file is absent from the evidence.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model]` covers a read through a symlink that leaves the project. The error delivered to the model names `src/escape.rs` and says \"outside\", the content is not leaked, the file is not recorded, and a second request is made.\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requests_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_are_denials]` and `unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors` cover denial across the `habeas` (line and item forms), `outline`, `ripgrep` and `list_files` tools. Each error mentions \"outside\", and no inputs are recorded.\n- `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` checks that `outline` on an ignored file returns an error naming the file and \"excluded\".\n\n**2. Discovery and search omit excluded files.**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[source_tools_share_sdk_visibility_for_untracked_files]` checks that `list_files`, `ripgrep` and `ast_grep` omit excluded files.\n  - The `list_files` listing contains only the visible entries.\n  - `ripgrep` and `ast_grep` return only `src/draft.rs`, and scoping them to the excluded file or directory gives empty results with no inputs.\n  - `outline` and `habeas` on the excluded file fail.\n- `search_records_nothing_clamps_at_eof_and_reports_failures` also shows an ignored hidden directory omitted from `ripgrep`, while a non-ignored hidden directory stays visible.\n- `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` shows that a site in a disallowed `private/notes.md` is omitted from the `references` results.\n\n**3. Malformed arguments and ordinary read failures return explanatory tool errors.**\n- `malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues` covers six cases:\n  - a non-integer `line_start`;\n  - a missing locator;\n  - a conflicting argument form;\n  - a missing file;\n  - an absent item;\n  - a line past EOF.\n  - Each failure is not `PermissionDenied`, is delivered in the second request, and leaves nothing in the evidence.\n- Argument validation errors are asserted in the tests for each tool:\n  - `ripgrep`: wrong types and unknown arguments in `search_records_nothing_clamps_at_eof_and_reports_failures`.\n  - `ast_grep`: language, rule and query errors in `ast_grep_returns_innermost_nodes_of_the_language_and_reports_failures`.\n  - `list_files`: `failed_listings_return_explanatory_tool_errors`.\n  - `outline`: `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs`.\n  - `references`: bad selections and roles in `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs`.\n  - `next_page`: a missing or unknown token in `paged_inputs_carry_their_definitions_and_deliver_only_their_own_inputs`.\n  - `github`: bad arguments in `additional_read_flow_searches_outlines_and_reads_a_rust_file`.\n- `operating_system_permission_failures_are_ordinary_read_failures` shows that OS permission errors are ordinary failures and not denials.\n\nThe tests that abort mandatory-input preparation are `disallowed_mandatory_inputs_abort_preparation` and the symlink and anchor tests in `src/authoring/inputs.rs`. They concern mandatory inputs rather than model tool reads. They add coverage of the denial reason but are not needed for adequacy.\n\nAll obligations in the requirement's text are mapped to tests with assertions on the outcome.",
  "references": "963cf9c62a49caeeb3abdcc3e89ee74bc9c0400a3a7d4b901a7cf8dc1478fb7c",
